flowchart TB
  accTitle: Why Harden-Runner has to see the DNS lookups of a job
  accDescr: A step or the runner looks up a host. When Harden-Runner answers, it notes the address of an allowed host and the connection passes. On a runner with GitHub's DNS experiment, so far in the region westus2, another resolver answers. Harden-Runner never sees the address and drops the connection, so the step fails and the runner hangs until the timeout of the job. Harden-Runner since v2.22.3, when its feature flags come within 3 seconds, and the step after it in every job with sudo take the experiment away.
  LOOKUP(["A step or the runner<br/>looks up a host"]) --> WHO{"Who answers?"}
  WHO -- "Harden-Runner" --> SEEN["It notes the address<br/>of an allowed host"]
  SEEN --> PASS["The connection passes"]
  WHO -- "GitHub's DNS experiment<br/>(region westus2)" --> HIDDEN["Harden-Runner never<br/>sees the address"]
  HIDDEN --> DROP["The connection is dropped:<br/>the step fails, and the runner<br/>hangs until the job's timeout"]
  FIX["Harden-Runner v2.22.3, and the step<br/>Let Harden-Runner see the DNS lookups<br/>in every job with sudo"] -. "take the<br/>experiment away" .-> WHO
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef problem fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
  class PASS done
  class DROP problem
